# SafeConnect Prototype

## Overview

The SafeConnect prototype demonstrates the proposed user experience for a community safety information and incident-reporting platform for the Auckland Park–Melville area in Johannesburg, South Africa.

The prototype was developed using Canva as part of the SafeConnect academic project for ILS2B01 Project Management.

## Access the Prototype

**Canva prototype:**  https://heyzazi.my.canva.site/safeconnect-auckland-park-prototype
https://canva.link/y2xvzon14gwvxtf  

The prototype is intended to demonstrate the proposed interface and user interactions. Access may depend on the sharing permissions configured in Canva.

## Key Features Demonstrated

The proposed platform explores the following features, where represented in the current prototype:

- Community safety information.
- Incident-reporting interface.
- High-priority safety alerts.
- Community snapshot and sample report information.
- Administrative review and moderation concepts.

Only features actually present in the current prototype should be described as demonstrated.

## Prototype Limitations

This is a visual, clickable prototype rather than a fully deployed production application. Sample incident information is for demonstration purposes and must not be interpreted as a verified real-world incident.

Live reporting, operational notifications, backend services, authentication, database integrations and real-world incident verification should not be assumed to be implemented.

## Future Improvements

Potential future work includes usability testing, accessibility improvements, refinement based on feedback, and further technical development if approved and supported by the project scope.